From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 21:29:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sched: add Infinity bounded-LIFO policy (default)

Extend the existing DRM scheduler policy switch with
 DRM_SCHED_POLICY_INFINITY (3), a select-side bounded-LIFO discipline in
 the KPP style: 7 head inserts + 1 tail insert per group of 8, O(1)
 mutating ops + bounded select scan (same bound as stock), with counter
 wrap forcing the tail. Selection scans the Infinity
list head-to-tail and picks the first ready, creditable entity, so a
blocked head never wedges the ring.

Discipline-native stats, per-drm_sched_rq plain u64 with no new locks:
 head/tail inserts at the Infinity insert hook, select hits, scan skips
 and ENOSPC stops at the select scan. Read-only debugfs infinity_drm
 (seq_file) sums at read across schedulers and run-queues and renders a
 small ASCII table.

Infinity is the default policy; pass sched_policy=1 on the kernel
command line (or via modprobe) to revert to FIFO. The RR/FIFO/FAIR
branches are left byte-identical, and the rb-tree stays empty on the
Infinity path.

Backport note (7.2.6): extends the in-tree policy switch in
drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler (sched_rq.c, sched_main.c, sched_internal.h,
sched_entity.c) and include/drm/gpu_scheduler.h. Debugfs-only stats,
no sysfs, Kconfig or .inc changes.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
